   "daf": "80a",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "(שַׁעֲוָה כְּדֵי לִיתֵּן עַל פִּי נֶקֶב קָטָן. תָּנָא: כְּדֵי לִיתֵּן עַל פִּי נֶקֶב קָטָן שֶׁל יַיִן.)",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: The measure that determines liability for carrying out «wax» is «equivalent» to that which is used «to place on the opening of a small hole» to seal it. A tanna «taught» in a Tosefta: «Enough to place on the opening of a small hole» in a receptacle holding «wine.» The size of a hole that enables pouring wine is smaller than the size of the hole required when pouring more viscous liquids."
  }
